      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060289
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-10-29T21:37:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s implementation specific, safe for reads, and undefined for writes. The docs in IMapper::lock (which is the HAL that underlies the call) are:\n\n```\nLocking the same buffer simultaneously from multiple threads is\npermitted, but if any of the threads attempt to lock the buffer for\nwriting, the behavior is undefined, except that it must not cause\nprocess termination or block the client indefinitely. Leaving the\nbuffer content in an indeterminate state or returning an error are both\nacceptable\n```",
      "parentUuid": "4a723e41_d7a32335",
      "revId": "3ec830380a6787e06fd0b8c1d5fd3d77397162d4",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    }
